wgestures (2.1.7ubuntu2) noble; urgency=high

  * Add the 4x4 middle-button quick panel on GNOME 46 Wayland and GTK3/X11.
  * Show four direct actions when an empty tile is right-clicked: launch an
    application, open a file, open a folder, or open an HTTP/HTTPS URL.
  * Keep configured-tile edit/delete actions and preserve existing right/X
    button gesture behavior while the panel is closed.
  * Honor "activate if running" on application tiles for the first time on
    GNOME Wayland and GTK3/X11 by matching /proc comm and raising the open
    window instead of spawning a duplicate.
  * Show each tile's description (or its type and target) as a tooltip.
  * Accept drag and drop on GTK3/X11 panel tiles: files, folders, .desktop
    launchers and web links dropped on an empty tile create matching entries
    and multiple drops fill consecutive free slots without overwriting.
  * Keep right and X button gestures working outside the open panel on GNOME
    Wayland and GTK3/X11; only presses on the panel surface are handed to the
    tiles (replayed natively so tile menus still work).
  * Cache installed-application records and tile icons so repeated panel
    opens no longer rescan every desktop file.
  * Let right and X button gestures keep working inside the slot editor's
    input fields on X11, fetch URL tile icons directly from the target site
    (cached under $XDG_CACHE_HOME/wgestures/favicons), and add a focus
    watchdog that closes the panel when an overlay swallows focus-out.
  * Warm the installed-application cache at daemon startup, skip panel
    config re-reads while the file is unchanged, and require the quick
    panel to have actually taken focus before the focus watchdog may
    close it (no more pop-up-then-vanish when focus is denied).
  * Reuse the GTK and GNOME tile trees on repeated opens, resolve application
    icons by Desktop ID, and let GNOME read URL favicons downloaded by the
    external wgestures helper instead of networking inside the compositor.
  * Keep the Xvfb acceptance result authoritative when a transient gvfs FUSE
    mount is still winding down during temporary-directory cleanup.
  * Fall back to Google's favicon compatibility endpoint when a target site
    rejects direct favicon clients (for example with HTTP 403), while keeping
    all network I/O in the external helper rather than GNOME Shell.
  * Toggle the quick panel on middle-button press on X11 and GNOME Wayland,
    reverting it if motion crosses the drag threshold, to match Windows and
    remove click-hold time from perceived latency.

